ENTRY       EC 2.7.1.1                  Enzyme
NAME        hexokinase;
            glucose kinase
CLASS       Transferases;
            Transferring phosphorus-containing groups;
            Phosphotransferases with an alcohol group as acceptor
SYSNAME     ATP:D-hexose 6-phosphotransferase
REACTION    ATP + D-hexose = ADP + D-hexose 6-phosphate
SUBSTRATE   ATP;
            D-hexose
PRODUCT     ADP;
            D-hexose 6-phosphate
COMMENT     D-glucose, D-mannose, D-fructose and sorbitol can act as
            acceptors; ITP and dATP can act as donors
PATHWAY     PATH: map00010  Glycolysis / Gluconeogenesis
            PATH: map00052  Galactose metabolism
ORTHOLOG    KO: K00844  hexokinase
GENES       HSA: 3098 3099 3101
            MMU: 15275 15277
DISEASE     MIM: 235700  Hexokinase deficiency
STRUCTURES  PDB: 1HKB 1HKC 1IG8
DBLINKS     ExplorEnz - The Enzyme Database: 2.7.1.1
            IUBMB Enzyme Nomenclature: 2.7.1.1
